vmwgfx: release surfaces and their backing buffers; look an import's buffer up once

Port of the host backend's fix. Every surface
this backend created or imported leaked, with the GEM handle of its backing
buffer, until the process exited: bo_destroy was GEM_CLOSE on a surface
(TTM base-object) handle, which fails with -EINVAL. Surface references are
counted per drm_file (one per PRIME_FD_TO_HANDLE plane, one per
GB_SURFACE_REF) and paid back per bo in bo_release. Imports look the backing
buffer up once; maps and CPU sync reuse it instead of taking a new reference
and GEM handle on every call. Plain GEM buffers are closed per handle and map
through MAP_DUMB.

--- a/vmwgfx.c
+++ b/vmwgfx.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
